---
description: QA and testing rules for reliability and fast feedback
version: 1.0.0
globs: ["tests/**", "qa/**", "apps/**/tests/**", "packages/**/tests/**", "**/*.spec.*", "**/*.test.*", "**/__tests__/**", "**/*.feature"]
alwaysApply: true
---

- Follow a test pyramid: many fast unit tests, fewer integration/contract tests, targeted e2e for critical paths.
- Keep tests deterministic and isolated; avoid shared state and real external dependencies without explicit fixtures.
- Use fixtures/builders over copy-paste; prefer table-driven cases to cover edge conditions.
- Mock only true boundaries; prefer contract tests for services over deep mocks.
- Add schema/contract tests for external integrations and block drift in CI (e.g., OpenAPI/GraphQL snapshots).
- Make failures actionable: clear assertions, minimal noise, stable snapshots with intent-revealing names.
- Run tests in CI with parallelism and caching; fail fast on flaky tests and quarantine only with owners/issue links.
- Track coverage trends but value meaningful assertions over raw percentages; ensure critical paths are exercised.
